l,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_translate":false},{"id":909224,"name":"Jubril Toheeb","username":"jubriltoheeb70","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.bubble.io/jubriltoheeb70/{size}/257752_2.png","created_at":"2023-08-12T05:45:04.627Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eIf I may ask, is the subscription process in a pop up or another page entirely?\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":9,"post_type":1,"posts_count":14,"updated_at":"2023-08-12T05:45:04.627Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":141,"readers_count":140,"score":48.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":276939,"topic_slug":"why-does-my-plugin-have-298-installs-but-only-12-month-in-payments","display_username":"Jubril Toheeb","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":70696,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/why-does-my-plugin-have-298-installs-but-only-12-month-in-payments/276939/9","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_translate":false},{"id":909264,"name":"Cory James","username":"GH5T","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.bubble.io/gh5t/{size}/209141_2.png","created_at":"2023-08-12T07:48:08.925Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"jubriltoheeb70\" data-post=\"8\" data-topic=\"276939\" data-full=\"true\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://sea1.discourse-cdn.com/bubble/user_avatar/forum.bubble.io/jubriltoheeb70/48/257752_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e jubriltoheeb70:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eProbably, they found a loophole on how to use it without subscription.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDoubt it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo be honest I blame their services (Bubble). They don’t produce accurate information about current installs, so why assume they have accurate information about universal installs?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe best way to keep track of your installs is to add an API inside your plugin to talk to your server. You can also get the app ID, last use time, etc.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI have 100’s of installs, but only a fraction are actually active installs. Not only that, I’ve seen it where I use a plugin on an app, duplicate it, then the amount of installs goes up, even if it’s a premium subbed plugin, and it’s not installed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI feel like they are about to revamp their contributor/reviewing/plugin/templating/stats system eventually, so I haven’t really said much about it.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":10,"post_type":1,"posts_count":14,"updated_at":"2023-08-12T07:48:41.881Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":8,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":137,"readers_count":136,"score":72.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":276939,"topic_slug":"why-does-my-plugin-have-298-installs-but-only-12-month-in-payments","display_username":"Cory James","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":fal